-- title:
--   Canonical orthogonal irreducible decomposition
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal E=\{p(x),|\psi_x\rangle^A\otimes|\sigma_x\rangle^C\}$ be a countably supported ensemble with strictly positive probabilities summing to one and normalized pure vectors on finite-dimensional complex systems $A,C$. Let $Y=y(X)$ be the canonical orthogonal irreducible-component label of the joint $AC$ ensemble. Entropies $S$ use base-two logarithms and refer to the resulting source and its canonical $Y$ extension.
--
--   Define $y(x)$ using the equivalence relation generated by nonzero inner products of the joint source vectors. Its nonempty fibers $X_y$ form an irreducible partition, and their spans $\mathcal F_y$ are pairwise orthogonal. The probabilities satisfy
--   $$q(y)=\sum_{x\in X_y}p(x)>0,\quad \sum_y q(y)=1,\quad p(x\mid y)=p(x)/q(y)\ (x\in X_y),\quad \sum_{x\in X_y}p(x\mid y)=1.$$
--   Consequently $q(y(x))p(x\mid y(x))=p(x)$. For any other partition $h:X\to Z$ into nonempty irreducible fibers with pairwise orthogonal spans, there is a bijection $e:Y\to Z$ such that $h=e\circ y$.
--
--   This identifies the canonical classical information used in the rate formulas.
-- source:
--   Entanglement-Assisted Quantum Data Compression, arXiv:1901.06346v1, PDF p. 2, Definition 2, following paragraph

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Advance50_P41

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Advance50.P41

open Filter

open scoped Topology BigOperators Matrix ComplexConjugate

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable Classical.decEq

variable {X A C : Type} [Fintype A] [Fintype C]

/-- Definition 2 and its following paragraph, PDF p.2: canonical orthogonal
irreducible decomposition, probability identities, and uniqueness up to
bijective relabeling of occupied components. -/
theorem irreducible_decomposition [Countable X] (s : ProductPureSource X A C) (hs : s.Valid) :
    s.IsDecomposition s.label ∧
    (∀ y : IrreducibleLabel s, 0 < s.componentProbability y ∧
      HasSum (fun x : {x // s.label x = y} => s.conditionalProbability y x.val) 1) ∧
    HasSum s.componentProbability 1 ∧
    (∀ x, s.componentProbability (s.label x) *
      s.conditionalProbability (s.label x) x = s.law.weight x) ∧
    (∀ (Y : Type) (h : X → Y), s.IsDecomposition h →
      ∃ e : IrreducibleLabel s ≃ Y, ∀ x, e (s.label x) = h x) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Advance50.P41

end
